```

This function takes an integer `n` as input and returns `True` if it is a prime number, and `False` otherwise. It first checks if `n` is less than or equal to 1, which means it is not prime. If `n` is 2, then it is prime. If `n` is even, then it is not prime. For all other values of `n`, the function checks if `n` is divisible by any odd number between 3 and its square root (inclusive). If it is divisible by any of these numbers, then it is not prime. Otherwise, it is prime.

